as been elected mayor of a small Peruvian Andes district with 229 votes \u2014 a 25-vote margin",
  "summary": "Hitler Mussolini Simeon Flores, 45, of the centre-left Ahora Naci\u00f3n party has been elected mayor of Queropalca, a remote district in the Peruvian Andes, winning 229 votes \u2014 25 more than his nearest rival, according to exit polls and data from Peru's elections office. The unusual pairing of forenames has drawn international attention to a district of barely 700 voters.",
  "body": [
   "A man named Hitler Mussolini Simeon Flores has been elected mayor of Queropalca, a remote district in Peru's central Hu\u00e1nuco region, securing a narrow victory in local elections reported on October 9.",
   "The 45-year-old, running for the centre-left Ahora Naci\u00f3n party, won 229 votes \u2014 about 34 percent of the ballots cast \u2014 finishing 25 votes ahead of his nearest rival, according to exit polls and data from Peru's elections office. A little over 700 people participated in the election in the Andean district, roughly 360 kilometres from Lima, where Flores was born.",
   "## An unusual name in the spotlight",
   "His two forenames are those of Adolf Hitler and Benito Mussolini, \"two of the most well-known figures of 20th-Century European totalitarian regimes,\" as the BBC put it \u2014 a coincidence that made his candidacy a \"striking event,\" according to local outlet Peru21.",
   "He is not the first Peruvian politician with such a name to win office. Hitler Guesclin Alba S\u00e1nchez was elected mayor of Y\u00fangar in 2018 after campaigning with the slogan \"I'm the good Hitler,\" and a candidate named Adolf Hitler Uunona won local elections in Namibia in 2020.",
   "The figures reported are from exit polls and preliminary elections-office data rather than certified final results; NewsVeria will update this story if the official proclamation differs."
  ],
