 {
  "id": "art-0065-jordan-jersey-14m-record-2026",
  "slug": "michael-jordan-1998-finals-jersey-sells-14-million-record",
  "headline": "Michael Jordan's 1998 NBA Finals Jersey Sells for Record $14 Million",
  "socialHeadline": "Michael Jordan's game-worn jersey from Game 2 of the 1998 NBA Finals just sold for $14M \u2014 a world record for basketball memorabilia",
  "summary": "A red Chicago Bulls road jersey worn by Michael Jordan during Game 2 of the 1998 NBA Finals has sold for $14 million in a private sale arranged by Hunt Auctions, setting a world record for basketball memorabilia and becoming the second-most expensive game-worn jersey ever sold.",
  "body": [
   "A game-worn Michael Jordan jersey from the 1998 NBA Finals has sold for $14 million, setting a world record for basketball memorabilia, auction house Hunt Auctions announced on Monday.",
   "The red Chicago Bulls road jersey was worn by Jordan in Game 2 of the 1998 Finals on June 5, 1998 \u2014 the famous 'Last Dance' series \u2014 when Chicago beat the Utah Jazz 93\u201388 in Chicago behind Jordan's 37 points. The jersey was photomatched to that game by authentication firms MeiGray and Sports Investors Authentication, confirming it is the exact garment Jordan wore that night.",
   "## A private sale, not an auction",
   "Unlike most headline memorabilia sales, this one did not go under the hammer. Hunt Auctions arranged the sale as a private treaty transaction, announcing the $14 million price on Monday. The buyer was identified as Ron Firman, a Miami-based real estate investor.",
   "The seller was a private collector who had purchased the jersey directly from the Chicago Bulls in 2003 and held it for more than two decades as the Finals' legend \u2014 and the memorabilia market \u2014 grew.",
   "## Second-highest jersey sale ever",
   "At $14 million, the Jordan jersey becomes the most expensive piece of basketball memorabilia ever sold and the second-most expensive game-worn jersey in any sport, behind only Babe Ruth's 1932 'called shot' Yankees jersey, which sold for $24.12 million in 2024.",
   "The sale continues a remarkable run for Jordan collectibles: his 1998 'Last Dance' Finals Game 1 jersey sold at Sotheby's in 2022 for $10.1 million, then a record for any game-worn sports item. That mark has now been comfortably eclipsed.",
   "## What remains unknown",
   "Hunt Auctions has not disclosed the full terms of the private sale beyond the price and the parties involved. NewsVeria will update this story if further details of the transaction are released."
  ],
  "category": "Sports",
  "tags": [
   "Michael Jordan",
   "NBA",
   "Chicago Bulls",
   "Auction",
   "Memorabilia",
   "Record"
  ],
