 {
  "id": "art-0066-lvmh-q3-sales-miss-2026",
  "slug": "lvmh-third-quarter-sales-miss-fashion-leather-decline-2026",
  "headline": "LVMH Third-Quarter Sales Miss Expectations as Fashion and Leather Division Shrinks",
  "socialHeadline": "LVMH's Q3 sales grew just 1% \u2014 below expectations \u2014 as its core fashion and leather division shrank 5%",
  "summary": "LVMH, the world's largest luxury group, reported third-quarter organic sales growth of just 1%, missing analyst expectations, as its flagship fashion and leather goods division posted a 5% organic decline amid a prolonged luxury slowdown.",
  "body": [
   "LVMH Mo\u00ebt Hennessy Louis Vuitton reported third-quarter organic revenue growth of just 1% on Monday, falling short of analyst expectations and underlining the strain on the luxury sector from a demand slowdown now in its third year.",
   "The result missed the 1.3% organic growth consensus compiled by Visible Alpha, according to Reuters. The disappointment was concentrated in the group's flagship fashion and leather goods division \u2014 home to Louis Vuitton and Dior \u2014 where organic sales fell 5%, far worse than the 1.8% decline analysts had expected.",
   "## First big luxury name to report",
   "LVMH is the first major luxury group to report third-quarter results, making its numbers a bellwether for the roughly $350 billion global luxury market. Rivals including Herm\u00e8s, Kering and Richemont report in the coming weeks, and investors will read LVMH's softness as a signal for the sector.",
   "The luxury industry has been grappling with weaker demand in China, cautious US consumers and a post-pandemic normalization after years of breakneck growth. LVMH's fashion and leather division is its largest profit engine, so a 5% organic contraction there carries outsized weight.",
   "## What the numbers agree on",
   "Both Reuters and CNA report the same key figures: 1% group organic growth against a 1.3% consensus, and a 5% organic decline in fashion and leather goods against a 1.8% expected fall. (The outlets differ on the absolute euro revenue figure, which NewsVeria is not publishing.)",
   "## What remains unknown",
   "LVMH did not break out regional performance in the initial reporting, and management commentary on the outlook for the holiday quarter will be closely watched. NewsVeria will update this story as peer results land."
  ],
  "category": "Business",
  "tags": [
