 {
  "id": "art-0067-fitbit-edge-launch-2026",
  "slug": "google-fitbit-edge-launch-price-specs-2026",
  "headline": "Google Launches $179.99 Fitbit Edge, Its First Repairable Fitness Tracker",
  "socialHeadline": "Google's new $179.99 Fitbit Edge sits between the Fitbit Air and Pixel Watch \u2014 and it's the company's first repairable tracker",
  "summary": "Google has launched the Fitbit Edge, a $179.99 fitness tracker positioned between the Fitbit Air and the Pixel Watch. It is Google's first repairable fitness tracker, with a modular design and replaceable battery, and it goes on sale October 27.",
  "body": [
   "Google on Monday unveiled the Fitbit Edge, a new $179.99 fitness tracker that slots into the middle of its wearables lineup \u2014 above the entry-level Fitbit Air and below the Pixel Watch. The device is available for pre-order now and hits shelves on October 27.",
   "The headline feature is repairability: the Fitbit Edge is Google's first fitness tracker built with a modular architecture and a replaceable battery, a notable shift for a category where devices have typically been sealed and disposable.",
   "## Specs and health features",
   "Google says the Edge delivers up to seven days of battery life, with a five-minute charge providing a full day of use. It carries 50-metre water resistance and GPS that Google claims is 40% more accurate than previous Fitbit devices.",
   "On the health side, the tracker auto-recognises 100 activities and offers more than 50 exercise modes. A new 'Health Guardian' feature tracks blood-pressure and insulin-resistance trends, and buyers get three months of Google Health Premium, including the Gemini-powered Google Health Coach.",
   "## Pricing and editions",
   "The standard Fitbit Edge costs $179.99 in four colours: Obsidian, Fog, Olive and Canyon. A Stephen Curry Special Edition is priced at $219.99.",
   "## The middle of the lineup",
   "The Edge's positioning is deliberate: a step up from the basic Fitbit Air for users who want richer health tracking, without the smartwatch price and complexity of the Pixel Watch. Whether the repairable design becomes a template for future Google wearables will be worth watching.",
   "## What remains unknown",
   "Independent reviews of battery life, GPS accuracy and the Health Guardian's trend measurements are not yet available. NewsVeria will update this story as review units are tested."
  ],
