 {
  "id": "art-0071-meta-muse-wonder-frontier-models-2026",
  "slug": "meta-muse-wonder-frontier-models-challenge-openai-anthropic",
  "headline": "Meta Unveils Muse Wonder Frontier AI Models, Taking Direct Aim at OpenAI and Anthropic",
  "socialHeadline": "Meta just launched Muse Wonder and Muse Wonder Full \u2014 its most capable AI models yet, built to rival OpenAI and Anthropic. Shares jumped ~4%.",
  "summary": "Meta on Monday introduced Muse Wonder and Muse Wonder Full, the first models in its Muse series, which the company calls its most capable AI models to date. The models target agentic tasks, coding and specialised domains like law, finance and health, and are positioned as a direct challenge to OpenAI and Anthropic \u2014 with Meta's shares rising about 4% on the news.",
  "body": [
   "Meta on Monday unveiled Muse Wonder and Muse Wonder Full, two frontier AI models the company described as its most capable to date, in its most aggressive push yet to compete with OpenAI and Anthropic in the race for leading artificial intelligence systems.",
   "In a blog post announcing the launch, Meta said the Muse Wonder series is designed to excel at agentic tasks \u2014 AI that can plan and act across multiple steps \u2014 as well as frontier-level coding and demanding specialist domains including law, finance and health. The company said the models introduce new capabilities called Active Memory and Active Focus.",
   "\"Fourteen months ago, we began an overhaul of our AI efforts, and in that time we've gone from rebuilding our foundations to pushing the frontier,\" the company said in the announcement.",
   "## Where the models will appear",
   "Meta said Muse Wonder is available starting Monday through the Meta Model API and Muse Code, and will power the company's Muse personal assistant \u2014 a product that launched in September \u2014 beginning with subscribers. Muse Wonder Full, the larger variant, is aimed at the most demanding workloads and will be available to Muse Code subscribers.",
   "The launch marks a decisive turn for Meta, which spent the past year reorganising and investing heavily in AI after acknowledging it had fallen behind rivals. Investors responded positively: Meta shares rose about 4% on Monday, according to Reuters.",
   "## What remains unknown",
   "Meta has not yet published full benchmark details or independent evaluations of the models, so claims of state-of-the-art performance remain the company's own until third parties test them. NewsVeria will update this story as independent results and availability details emerge."
  ],
  "category": "Artificial Intelligence",
  "tags": [
