 {
  "id": "art-0072-uk-iran-raf-fairford-sanctions-2026",
  "slug": "uk-blames-iran-raf-fairford-incident-sanctions-two-nationals",
  "headline": "UK Says Iran Likely Behind RAF Fairford Incident, Sanctions Two Iranian Nationals",
  "socialHeadline": "Britain says the September incident at RAF Fairford was \"highly likely\" coordinated by Iran \u2014 sanctioning two Iranian nationals and summoning Tehran's ambassador.",
  "summary": "Prime Minister Andy Burnham told parliament on Monday that the 27 September incident at RAF Fairford was \"highly likely\" coordinated in Iran and \"almost certainly\" directed by Iran's Islamic Revolutionary Guard. Foreign Secretary Ed Miliband summoned Iran's ambassador and sanctioned two Iranian nationals with asset freezes and travel bans; Iran denied involvement.",
  "body": [
   "The United Kingdom on Monday formally blamed Iran for an incident at RAF Fairford on 27 September, with Prime Minister Andy Burnham telling the House of Commons that the episode was \"highly likely to have been co-ordinated in Iran, almost certainly directed by Iran's Islamic Revolutionary Guard.\"",
   "\"We will not tolerate these threats on our soil,\" Burnham said, announcing the government's response to the incident at the Gloucestershire airbase, which is used by the United States Air Force.",
   "## Sanctions and summons",
   "Foreign Secretary Ed Miliband summoned Iran's ambassador to London on Monday, and the government designated two Iranian nationals under the 2023 Iran Sanctions Regulations: Ruhollah Bazghandi, described as head of counterespionage operations within the Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps, and Shahram Ali Reza Tamarzadeh Jakki, described as a facilitator of the Zindashti criminal network. Both face immediate asset freezes, travel bans and director disqualification.",
   "The government said it has designated the IRGC under its state-threats powers and has now sanctioned more than 550 Iranian individuals and entities.",
   "## What happened at the base",
   "Seven men \u2014 six British nationals and one dual UK-Iranian national, all in their twenties \u2014 were arrested over the 27 September incident at RAF Fairford and later released on bail; none has been charged. Police found petrol and gasoline at the scene but no explosives, according to the government's account. About 29 countries joined a US-led statement condemning the incident.",
   "## What remains unknown",
   "The attribution is the UK government's stated assessment; Iran's ambassador reiterated Tehran's denial of involvement when summoned. No charges have been filed against the seven suspects, and no fuller public account of the plot has been released. NewsVeria will update this story as official findings or court proceedings emerge."
  ],
  "category": "World",
  "tags": [
