 {
  "id": "art-0073-france-supermarket-cyberattack-fridges-2026",
  "slug": "france-supermarket-cyberattack-refrigeration-shutdown",
  "headline": "Hackers Take Over Refrigeration Systems at Hundreds of French Supermarkets in 'Unprecedented' Cyberattack",
  "socialHeadline": "An \"unprecedented\" cyberattack hijacked fridges at hundreds of French supermarkets overnight, heating them to 50\u00b0C and spoiling food across the country.",
  "summary": "A cyberattack overnight crippled refrigeration systems at hundreds of supermarkets across France, forcing stores to discard spoiled food. Coop\u00e9rative U's president called it \"unprecedented\", Intermarch\u00e9 and Leclerc confirmed outages, and the Paris prosecutor opened an investigation. Attackers hijacked older equipment controllers to force defrosting; no culprits have been identified.",
  "body": [
   "A large-scale cyberattack overnight targeted the refrigeration systems of major French supermarket chains, shutting down fridges across hundreds of stores and forcing retailers to throw away spoiled fresh and frozen food on Monday.",
   "Dominique Schelcher, president of Coop\u00e9rative U, confirmed the attack on social media, saying: \"Targeting equipment essential to the preservation of fresh products and to the food supply of the French people is of extreme gravity and is unprecedented. It is unacceptable.\"",
   "## Scope of the outages",
   "Intermarch\u00e9, owned by Groupement Les Mousquetaires, said through a spokesperson that \"some fresh and frozen food display units are out of service\" and that affected products had been removed from sale. Several E. Leclerc stores also confirmed outages. Trade outlets reported Carrefour and Monoprix stores affected, though those companies had not confirmed it as of Monday. Published counts vary: Intermarch\u00e9/Netto figures range from roughly 150 to at least 300 stores, and more than 100 Coop\u00e9rative U outlets reported problems.",
   "## How the attack worked",
   "According to cybersecurity reporting on the companies' statements, the attackers hijacked older Danfoss AK-SM 8xxA refrigeration controllers, triggering forced defrosting cycles that heated units to about 50 degrees Celsius for around six hours. The Paris prosecutor's office said it had opened an investigation into \"the large-scale cyberattack affecting the refrigerators of several major food retail chains across France.\" France's ANSSI cybersecurity agency is involved, and the matter has reached Prime Minister S\u00e9bastien Lecornu's office.",
   "## What remains unknown",
   "The attackers have not been identified and no group has claimed responsibility; the story should not attribute the attack to any actor. Store counts and financial-loss figures differ between outlets and remain estimates, not official figures. Ahold Delhaize reported an unrelated \"security issue\" on the same day, with no confirmed link. NewsVeria will update this story as the investigation develops."
  ],
  "category": "Technology",
