 {
  "id": "art-0074-dc-golf-course-trees-ruling-2026",
  "slug": "judge-blocks-further-tree-cutting-dc-golf-course",
  "headline": "Federal Judge Halts Tree Cutting at D.C. Golf Course After Blistering Rebuke of Justice Department",
  "socialHeadline": "A federal judge ordered a halt to tree-cutting at a D.C. golf course after ~430 trees were felled over the weekend \u2014 \"I am just beyond disappointed with the government.\"",
  "summary": "U.S. District Judge Ana C. Reyes ordered a temporary halt to tree removal at East Potomac Golf Links after the government acknowledged about 430 trees were cut over the weekend. In an emergency hearing Monday, Reyes rebuked Justice Department lawyers, saying the move \"cost the government all of its credibility\"; no sanctions were imposed.",
  "body": [
   "A federal judge on Monday ordered an immediate halt to tree-cutting at East Potomac Golf Links in Washington, D.C., after the government acknowledged that roughly 430 trees had been felled there over the weekend \u2014 and delivered a blistering rebuke to the Justice Department lawyers defending the move.",
   "U.S. District Judge Ana C. Reyes, presiding over an emergency hearing in the case DC Preservation League v. Department of Interior, said the cutting had \"cost the government all of its credibility.\"",
   "\"More than just being upset and furious right now, I am just beyond disappointed with the government,\" Reyes said, according to courtroom reporting. \"No, you did your absolute worst.\" She added: \"Ignorance is not an excuse\" and \"I am thoroughly unamused right now.\"",
   "## What happened",
   "The trees were cut on Saturday, 10 October, after the government gave notice at 4:55 p.m. on Friday. The government acknowledged about 430 trees removed; the plaintiffs, who are suing over the National Park Service's management of the Hains Point course, claimed the number was 529 \u2014 matching the plan's target of up to 529 removals, with roughly 300 more planned. Reyes had previously required advance notice for tree removals in the case.",
   "Reyes ordered National Park Service Superintendent Kevin Griess to testify and imposed a halt on further cutting through 13 October, warning of contempt proceedings for any violation. Justice Department lawyer Marissa Piropato represented the government at the hearing.",
   "## What remains unknown",
   "No sanctions were imposed on the government \u2014 only the temporary halt and the contempt warning, so this story does not claim otherwise. The halt could be extended at a further hearing, and the underlying lawsuit continues. NewsVeria will update this story if the order is extended."
  ],
  "category": "US",
  "tags": [
   "Washington DC",
   "Golf course",
   "Federal court",
   "Ana Reyes",
   "Justice Department",
   "Environment"
  ],
