 {
  "id": "art-0075-bumble-go-private-1bn-2026",
  "slug": "bumble-advanced-talks-go-private-1-billion",
  "headline": "Bumble in Advanced Talks to Go Private at About $1 Billion, Reports Say",
  "socialHeadline": "Dating app Bumble is reportedly in advanced talks to go private at ~$1B \u2014 about triple its current market value. Neither company has commented.",
  "summary": "Bumble is in advanced talks to be taken private by Ithaca Holdings at a valuation of about $1 billion, Reuters and The Wall Street Journal reported Monday, each citing its own sourcing. A deal could come as soon as this week, but neither company commented and the talks could still fall apart.",
  "body": [
   "Dating app Bumble is in advanced talks to go private at a valuation of roughly $1 billion, Reuters and The Wall Street Journal reported on Monday, in a deal that would value the company at about triple its recent market capitalisation.",
   "Reuters, citing a source familiar with the matter, reported that the buyer in talks is Ithaca Holdings and that a transaction could be announced as soon as this week. The Journal confirmed the talks with its own sourcing. Neither Bumble nor Ithaca responded to requests for comment.",
   "The reported $1 billion valuation compares with a market value of roughly $335\u2013389 million on Friday. Bumble's shares jumped in afternoon trading on the reports.",
   "## The buyer and the stakes",
   "Ithaca Holdings was founded by Ravi Gupta, a Sequoia partner and former Instacart finance chief, and John Hegeman, a former Meta chief revenue officer. Founder Whitney Wolfe Herd \u2014 who returned as chief executive in March 2025 \u2014 is expected to roll part of her stake and remain involved, according to the reports. Private-equity firm Blackstone holds about a 14% stake, per FactSet, and Morgan Stanley ran an earlier sale process for the company.",
   "Bumble, based in Austin, Texas, went public in 2021 at a valuation above $14 billion but has struggled since, cutting about 30% of its staff in 2025 as growth stalled.",
   "## What remains unknown",
   "The talks are advanced but not final: both outlets cautioned a deal could still collapse, and neither company has commented. Until a transaction is announced, this story treats the takeover as reported talks, not a done deal. NewsVeria will update if an agreement is confirmed."
  ],
  "category": "Business",
  "tags": [
   "Bumble",
   "M&A",
   "Take-private",
   "Ithaca Holdings",
   "Dating apps",
   "Tech business"
  ],
