 {
  "id": "art-0076-renoir-paintings-recovered-france-2026",
  "slug": "stolen-renoir-paintings-found-behind-wall-france",
  "headline": "Two Stolen Renoir Paintings Found Behind a Wall in France, Prosecutor Says",
  "socialHeadline": "Two stolen Renoir paintings worth ~\u20ac4.2M were found hidden behind a cinderblock wall in France, a month after the museum heist. Four men charged.",
  "summary": "French police have recovered two Renoir paintings stolen from the Mus\u00e9e Renoir in Cagnes-sur-Mer last month, finding them hidden behind a false wall in a house in Clermont-l'H\u00e9rault. Six suspects were arrested and four men charged; the works, valued at about \u20ac4.2 million, were damaged and need restoration.",
  "body": [
   "French police have recovered two paintings by Pierre-Auguste Renoir that were stolen from a museum on the French Riviera last month, finding them hidden behind a solid false wall in a house hundreds of kilometres away, prosecutors said Monday.",
   "\"The paintings were hidden behind a solid cinderblock wall. They were completely undetectable,\" Marseille prosecutor Nicolas Bessone told reporters at a press conference.",
   "## The theft and the recovery",
   "The two works \u2014 \"Madame Colonna Romano\" (also known as Portrait of Madame Colonna Romano) and \"Young Woman at the Well\" (1886) \u2014 were taken on 8 September from the Mus\u00e9e Renoir in Cagnes-sur-Mer, where they had been on loan from the Mus\u00e9e d'Orsay since 1995. The thieves cut a garden fence and entered through a window, initially seizing four works but abandoning two \u2014 \"Madame Pichon\" and \"Coco lisant\" \u2014 in the museum gardens.",
   "Police recovered the two Renoirs on 8 October from a laundry room beneath a staircase in a house in Clermont-l'H\u00e9rault, concealed behind a plasterboard and cinderblock false wall. The paintings, together valued at about \u20ac4.2 million ($4.7 million) according to Reuters, were damaged and will need restoration before returning to public view.",
   "## Arrests and charges",
   "Six people were arrested earlier in the week, and four men were charged between 10 and 12 October, including a 29-year-old principal suspect who was charged after a DNA match. Two other suspects were released. Bessone said the arrests were accelerated over fears the group was planning a second museum raid, reportedly targeting the Fondation Maeght.",
   "\"I did not believe the principal suspect visited that museum simply out of a love of art,\" Bessone said, according to Reuters.",
   "## What remains unknown",
   "Reporting identifies the suspects only by age and status \u2014 no names have been published, and this story follows the same restraint. The investigation continues, and the paintings have been moved to Marseille's Interdisciplinary Center for Conservation and Restoration, according to the Culture Ministry. NewsVeria will update this story if further charges are filed."
  ],
  "category": "Entertainment",
  "tags": [
   "Renoir",
   "Art theft",
   "France",
   "Museum",
   "Paintings",
   "Cagnes-sur-Mer"
  ],
