 {
  "author": "NewsVeria Newsroom",
  "body": [
   "RJ Mitte, the actor best known for portraying Walter White Jr. on the acclaimed television drama 'Breaking Bad', has died at the age of 34. News of his death in Brownsville, Texas, on Monday was confirmed in a statement released through the talent management agency that represented him.",
   "The statement described him as a beloved actor, philanthropist and passionate disability rights advocate, and said he had brought authenticity to the role while building a platform on disability awareness and inclusion. No details about the circumstances of his death were given.",
   "## A breakthrough role informed by real life",
   "Mitte, who lived with cerebral palsy from childhood, was cast as Walter 'Flynn' White Jr., the teenage son of Bryan Cranston's Walter White, across all five seasons of AMC's 'Breaking Bad' (2008\u20132013). His personal experience informed the performance of a character who used crutches and whose storyline grew more prominent as the series built to its conclusion.",
   "He went on to appear in the ABC Family drama 'Switched at Birth', the Netflix series 'The Guardians of Justice', and the 2021 coming-of-age film 'Triumph', in which he played a high school wrestler with cerebral palsy \u2014 a role he also executive produced.",
   "## An advocate off screen",
   "Beyond acting, Mitte worked as a Screen Actors Guild spokesperson for performers with disabilities and served as a celebrity ambassador for United Cerebral Palsy and Shriners Children's. He also led The Mitte Foundation, supporting philanthropic and community initiatives, and asked \u2014 through his representatives \u2014 that the privacy of his family and close ones be respected.",
   "USA Today reported that Mitte was declared dead at 1:32 p.m. local time at his residence, citing Cameron County Justice of the Peace Judge Cyndi Hinojosa. CNN reported that a spokesperson for the justice of the peace's office said the death was under investigation and that no foul play was suspected at this time.",
   "## Tributes",
   "Fellow 'Breaking Bad' cast members remembered him warmly, with Dean Norris \u2014 who played Hank Schrader \u2014 calling him a sweetheart of a young man who will be greatly missed, according to The Times. NewsVeria will update this story in place if his representatives release further information."
  ],
